                        ],
                        "form": "бесконта́ктна"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e6476f89-23eb-49f2-8d5c-dd265b3df6a9",
                        "entry_id": "eb42b0b0-17bf-3346-9291-82c955ca147b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "бесконта́ктны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d7556415-c893-3efb-ae5d-a6c878480d61",
                        "entry_id": "eb42b0b0-17bf-3346-9291-82c955ca147b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "не имеющий контактов в электрических цепях, питающих электропривод"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8ec6e3cb-f736-3f09-a70f-6f24a54e2f2c",
                        "entry_id": "eb42b0b0-17bf-3346-9291-82c955ca147b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "осуществляемый без непосредственного физического контакта"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ffd7712-d177-4cc8-8a6b-2a4e70382f0b",
                                "sense_id": "8ec6e3cb-f736-3f09-a70f-6f24a54e2f2c",
                                "text": "Да, это идеальный вариант для бесконтактных соревнований, когда удар нужно останавливать у цели ― но не для реального боя ногами."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2498180-7ecc-448b-9a54-5622c001d39b",
                                "sense_id": "8ec6e3cb-f736-3f09-a70f-6f24a54e2f2c",
                                "text": "Худые, пузатые, плешивые и чубатые, они терлись об нее в танго и вальсе, с неудовольствием переходя в бесконтактный танец."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6541f886-ac9f-437d-9ad0-0ccc33a7d686",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb42b0b0-17bf-3346-9291-82c955ca147b",
                        "target_lang_word": "contactless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contactless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b9d88c2-818a-392a-a34c-55ebd5a7393f",
                                        "entry_id": "0aa44720-2578-3ce2-994b-c2c4e96854cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That does not use or require contact in order to happen or operate.",
                                            "Conducted without human-to-human contact to improve ease of use or reduce the potential spread of a contagious disease; contact-free."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85f5e8c2-1b22-47af-a695-7fb2007a4ba2",
                                                "sense_id": "2b9d88c2-818a-392a-a34c-55ebd5a7393f",
                                                "text": "Contactless commerce, of which Amazon Go is at the extreme end, was of course already by the autumn of 2019 a growing trend, what with increasing numbers of self-checkout counters and websites and apps that allowed us to have everything from groceries to pet supplies to prescription medication delivered right to our doorsteps."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7328cdf2-73e4-49d7-a69b-cd90b1344a80",
                                                "sense_id": "2b9d88c2-818a-392a-a34c-55ebd5a7393f",
                                                "text": "Please stay in touch with me / In this contactless society / Anywhere that you may be"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "182cb6d7-dfd2-353b-a687-564cc64c886a",
                                        "entry_id": "0aa44720-2578-3ce2-994b-c2c4e96854cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That does not use or require contact in order to happen or operate.",
                                            "Happening without physical contact at the point of sale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2886cad2-31b7-4ae5-a73f-2264b3fa3ad2",
                                                "sense_id": "182cb6d7-dfd2-353b-a687-564cc64c886a",
                                                "text": "TfL has been saying for a few years that Oyster will eventually be withdrawn, but not until contactless payments can offer railcard discounts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99ca79b7-2ea5-36fd-9101-dde42ba64474",
                                        "entry_id": "0aa44720-2578-3ce2-994b-c2c4e96854cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That has no contact or contacts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "contactless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cf6dfe6-ba35-37b8-ba22-3e10c6411d9f",
                                        "entry_id": "f2d0cdfc-c5c4-35a1-85db-f83739514a8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A technology for paying for goods etc. while physically present at the point of interaction but without the need for physical contact."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09253366-28b9-43f7-bef1-36fd84b14d71",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf6dfe6-ba35-37b8-ba22-3e10c6411d9f",
                                                "text": "The motivation for using contactless is clear: it is most popular for people in a rush (58 per cent), people with a queue behind them (30 per cent) and those in busy places with lots of people (26 per cent)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0148a20-04c0-4cdf-8506-5bab4e537148",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf6dfe6-ba35-37b8-ba22-3e10c6411d9f",
                                                "text": "Even before the coronavirus struck, contactless was starting to become our way of life, our active choice."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
